# Expense Claims — Proposed Test Cases (Azure DevOps convention)

> Proposal for new test cases in test plan **Release testing: mysdworx app master** (ID 1132029).
> Format mirrors the existing convention observed in suites **7 - Expenses** (requester) and
> **9.2 - Expenses / 9.2.1 Standard** (approver): `Code - Category: As a <role> I can <action>
> [payrollEngine][platform]`, steps as **Action → Expected** with `-`-bulleted UI checks.
> Grounded in `Claim_FunctionalDoc_Requester`, `Claim_FunctionalDoc_Approver`, `Claim_APIdoc`.

## Suite placement (proposed)
- **Requester:** add under **7 - Expenses** using the existing `[Claims]` prefix (there are already
  two: *[Claims] As a user I can open expense tile (overview)* [1336230] and *[Claims] As a user I
  can check claims which were rejected* [1336246]). Optionally group into a child suite **7.1 - Expense Claims**.
- **Approver:** add a new child suite under **9 - Pending Approvals**, e.g. **9.5 - Expense Claims**
  (mirrors 9.2 - Expenses with 9.5.1 Standard / 9.5.2 Notifications / 9.5.3 Newsfeed items).

## Markers (from the Claims test-case notes)
- **[MOCK]** — needs an HTTP Toolkit Modify rule to force a flag/state/error.
- **[2-ROLE]** — needs both requester and approver accounts.
- **(gap)** — behaviour not fully specified in the wiki; verify empirically.
- Payroll tags `[eBloxHR,HRSS]`; platform tags `[Android,iOS]` where UI-interaction differs.

