# Approver — proposed suite **9.5 - Expense Claims**

### 9.5A - As a manager user I can open the Claims approvals overview [eBloxHR,HRSS]
**Priority:** P1
| # | Action | Expected |
|--|--|--|
| 1 | User taps **Pending Approvals**. *Test with a single approval category and with multiple categories* | - single category → **Claims approvals overview** directly; multiple → categories overview first, then select **Claims** |
| 2 | User views the overview | - list of approval cards (one per submitted claim), scrollable; each card shows **employee name**, **total amount** (one/multiple currencies), **claim date**, and inline **Approve/Reject** |
| 3 | No claims awaiting approval | - **empty state** shown |

### 9.5B - As a manager user I can approve a claim inline from the overview [eBloxHR,HRSS][Android,iOS]
**Priority:** P1
| # | Action | Expected |
|--|--|--|
| 1 | On a pending claim card, user taps **Approve** | - approver-comment step appears per config (see 9.5F); approve is always **full-claim** |
| 2 | User confirms | - entire claim **approved**; claim **removed** from pending approvals; success toast at top of list |
| 3 | Requester side **[2-ROLE]** | - claim state updates to **Approved** on the requester UI |

### 9.5C - As a manager user I can reject a claim inline from the overview (full-claim) [eBloxHR,HRSS][Android,iOS]
**Priority:** P1
| # | Action | Expected |
|--|--|--|
| 1 | On a pending claim card, user taps **Reject** | - **approver comment** screen opens; scope is **full-claim** (no expense selection from overview) |
| 2 | User enters a reason and confirms | - claim **rejected/returned** to employee; removed from pending approvals; success toast |
| 3 | User verifies the selection screen is **not** reachable here | - partial-reject expense selection is **only** available from claim detail (see 9.5E) |

### 9.5D - As a manager user I can approve a claim from the detail screen [eBloxHR,HRSS]
**Priority:** P2
| # | Action | Expected |
|--|--|--|
| 1 | User taps a claim card body → **claim detail (approval context)** | - reuses the employee claim-detail layout; **header shows no actions**; bottom bar shows **Approve** / **Reject** while Pending |
| 2 | User taps **Approve** → confirms (comment per config) | - entire claim approved; on success returns to the list; claim removed from pending |
| 3 | Backend/network failure from detail **[MOCK]** | - manager stays on the detail screen; fail toast; claim **remains pending** |

### 9.5E - As a manager user I can reject a claim partially from detail [eBloxHR,HRSS]
**Priority:** P1
| # | Action | Expected |
|--|--|--|
| 1 | From claim **detail**, user taps **Reject** | - **assigned-expense rejection selection** screen opens (only reachable from detail) |
| 2 | User selects invalid expenses | - multiple selectable; selection **visually explicit**; **selected = rejected, unselected = approved** |
| 3 | User tries to continue with **zero** selected | - cannot proceed; must select **≥1** |
| 4 | User taps **Cancel/Back** | - abandons; returns to detail with **no changes** |
| 5 | User continues → enters reason → confirms | - selected expenses **rejected**; claim **returned** to employee with partial selection; removed from pending |

